      "rev_n_1_ecf7bc_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_ecf7bc_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_ecf7bc",
        "thought_text": "Instead of brute-forcing through all possible values of n and k, we can use a more efficient approach by analyzing the pattern of stolen chocolates. The key observation is that the number of ways m is related to the sum of geometric series, which allows us to solve this problem more quickly.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_ecf7bc_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_331fd635dd",
        "created_at": 1794529159.076914
      },
      "rev_n_2_c31cc3_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_c31cc3_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_c31cc3",
        "thought_text": "Instead of iterating through all possible k values for each n, we can use a more efficient approach by observing the pattern of ways as n increases. The number of ways grows exponentially with n, so we can use binary search to find the smallest n that satisfies the condition. This approach will significantly reduce the time complexity and avoid the TLE error.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_c31cc3_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_d939ea33f9",
        "created_at": 1794529221.2924845
      },
      "rev_n_3_4a030e_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_4a030e_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_4a030e",
        "thought_text": "Instead of iterating through all possible k values for each n, we can use a more efficient approach by observing the pattern of ways the thieves can steal chocolates. The key insight is that the number of ways increases more rapidly as n increases, allowing us to use binary search more effectively.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_4a030e_0",
